      "Language": "pol",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Pyralgin (metamizole sodium) usefulness was tested in premedication of 90 patients subjected to processing of hard tooth tissues by grinding or drilling. The results of the study demonstrated that about 2/3 of the patients failed to observe any difference in the painfulness of the procedure with and without premedication with Pyralgin. In 1/3 of the patients Pyralgin reduced pain, improved wellbeing and raised the emotional status during the procedure. This effect might be regarded as a placebo result."},
